{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:23Z","created_by_operation":"op_f060b71e559d4d188045e24b0c2ec514","id":"pg_8f77661e0b28598dba717d4d4ea55796","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/vibe-stack-ggez-runtime-architecture-md-45ed541cb163-7d4d4ea55796.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_95ead35ff53c5399b358ca1db90ba348"],"title":"vibe-stack/ggez/RUNTIME_ARCHITECTURE.md @ 45ed541cb163","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:23Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f060b71e559d4d188045e24b0c2ec514"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_18f9c0a16daae8fc5dee7bc0d75dd459ffbf9e1699bc8481b52fdc8f94d4ca5e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"ARCHITECTURE.md appears to be an AI-generated specification document (it addresses a coding agent and offers further help), so its contents are design intent rather than verified implemented behavior."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7bf47cf6c7988db929c7e14d6a8ec7b1bdcba6da63b75e5e956bfbe9df89b743"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The spec's editor core separates authoring state from React: a SceneDocument (nodes, entities, materials, assets, layers) with CommandStack, Selection, and EventBus, where React must not store geometry state."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8874c4fc8493ab77708eba589b0cdba48c3fe2800e3b2f0b54cf1af6e7db3b79"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The spec's stack lists Vite/React/TypeScript, three with @react-three/fiber and drei, earcut and clipper2-ts, three-mesh-bvh, valtio and xstate, plus Web Workers via comlink."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d0b889d521d7f6c6b87974348fef8299c2e0887cfe7533787672b4ab70353c0d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The spec defines a JSON-based .whmap editor save format and an export pipeline targeting GLTF and an engine format (USD optional) with transform baking, mesh merging, and collision generation."},{"claim_ids":["clm_df00c99db16ffbaac144f4c1cf6b3260da08031d1389b6eca92a7af37a2b2304"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The spec calls for a half-edge mesh structure (vertex, twin, next, face) enabling edge traversal, loop selection, face extrusion, and vertex editing, with earcut triangulation for rendering."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f736a5309c7206c1b67f509ed4a71f63b2edb71839349a96effa6331c983690c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The editor spec targets a browser-based Source-2-style level editor with brush solids, editable meshes, and instanced models, optimized for rapid blockout and iteration in the Hammer/Radiant/TrenchBroom lineage."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f9588202b54036b98a3a465277cdb8bf6e34528857c9af585b53c2d839eb4118"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Brushes are specified as convex solids defined by plane half-spaces (not vertex meshes), with faces derived from planes and reconstruction via triple-plane intersection, inside tests, and angle-sorted face vertices."}],"claim_ids":["clm_18f9c0a16daae8fc5dee7bc0d75dd459ffbf9e1699bc8481b52fdc8f94d4ca5e","clm_7bf47cf6c7988db929c7e14d6a8ec7b1bdcba6da63b75e5e956bfbe9df89b743","clm_8874c4fc8493ab77708eba589b0cdba48c3fe2800e3b2f0b54cf1af6e7db3b79","clm_d0b889d521d7f6c6b87974348fef8299c2e0887cfe7533787672b4ab70353c0d","clm_df00c99db16ffbaac144f4c1cf6b3260da08031d1389b6eca92a7af37a2b2304","clm_f736a5309c7206c1b67f509ed4a71f63b2edb71839349a96effa6331c983690c","clm_f9588202b54036b98a3a465277cdb8bf6e34528857c9af585b53c2d839eb4118"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:23Z","created_by_operation":"op_f060b71e559d4d188045e24b0c2ec514","id":"pg_9580dfa988635b278ff56f83246482a0","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/vibe-stack-ggez-architecture-md-45ed541cb163-6f83246482a0.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_731870357a8550ed8bdfa12dfc9d9b3d"],"title":"vibe-stack/ggez/ARCHITECTURE.md @ 45ed541cb163","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:23Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f060b71e559d4d188045e24b0c2ec514"}
